      the partners send no System Name TLV, not because the DUT cannot show one.
  => STEP 2 PASS: the DUT received the frames and built the neighbour entry out of the
     fields the frames carried.  Five chosen values came back unchanged, the frame count
     matched exactly, and the entry landed on the right port only.

STEP 3 -- `no lldp transmit` stops the frames, and only the frames             PASS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Method: `lldp transmit` and `lldp receive` are separate per-interface commands.  This
  step removes transmit and proves the frames stop.  Reception on the same port is the
  control: it must keep working, which proves the link, the capture and LLDP itself are
  all still alive.

awplus#configure terminal
awplus(config)#interface port1.0.10
awplus(config-if)#no lldp transmit
awplus(config-if)#end
