STEP 10 -- LLDP notifications are real SNMP traps, and the per-port switch gates them  PASS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Method: a notification is the one LLDP output that leaves the device by a path no show
  command can describe.  So the trap is caught on the wire and its varbinds are read.
  The control is the same stimulus with notifications off.

  Baseline first.  The SNMP agent was already on and nothing else was configured:
awplus#show running-config | include snmp
    snmp-server
awplus#show snmp-server
    SNMP Server .......................... Enabled

awplus(config)#snmp-server community cklldp ro
awplus(config)#snmp-server host 10.38.22.33 version 2c cklldp
awplus(config)#snmp-server enable trap lldp
awplus(config)#interface port1.0.10
