awplus#show running-config | include snmp
    snmp-server
    snmp-server enable trap lldp
    snmp-server community cklldp
    snmp-server host 10.38.22.33 version 2c cklldp
awplus#show lldp interface port1.0.10
     1.0.10   Rx Tx  RC --  10.38.22.34      ---------- -------- -------- McNpLoPe--

  <-- `RC` in the Notif column means LLDP Remote Tables Change notifications are on for
      this port.
  <-- Two CLI storage facts, both read back here.  `snmp-server community cklldp ro` is
      stored as `snmp-server community cklldp`, because `ro` is the default and is not
      written back.  `lldp notification` is stored as `lldp notifications`, plural.  A
      later search of the running-config for the singular form finds nothing.

  Three deliberate neighbour-table changes were driven from the host, inside a 60 s
  capture of UDP port 162 on eth3:

    box local   stimulus
    15:27:21    2 frames, chassis 02:00:00:00:00:bb, port-id ckNOTIF   -- an insert
    15:27:26    1 shutdown frame (TTL 0) for the same chassis          -- a delete
    15:27:45    2 frames, chassis 02:00:00:00:00:cc, port-id ckNOTIF2  -- another insert

tb277$ tools/tb tool tb277 lldp1159 snmpwire /tmp/lldp1159/s10_trap.pcap --port 162 --values --abs
    #1   15:27:26.385 10.38.22.34:48414 -> 10.38.22.33:162  SNMPv2c  community='cklldp' pdu=SNMPv2-Trap
          1.3.6.1.2.1.1.3.0 = TimeTicks: 1623624
          1.3.6.1.6.3.1.1.4.1.0 = OID: 1.0.8802.1.1.2.0.0.1
          1.0.8802.1.1.2.1.2.2.0 = Gauge32: 9        <- lldpStatsRemTablesInserts
          1.0.8802.1.1.2.1.2.3.0 = Gauge32: 4        <- lldpStatsRemTablesDeletes
          1.0.8802.1.1.2.1.2.4.0 = Gauge32: 0        <- lldpStatsRemTablesDrops
          1.0.8802.1.1.2.1.2.5.0 = Gauge32: 3        <- lldpStatsRemTablesAgeouts
    #2   15:27:32.100 ... Inserts: 9   Deletes: 5   Drops: 0   Ageouts: 3
    #3   15:27:50.289 ... Inserts: 10  Deletes: 5   Drops: 0   Ageouts: 3
    SUMMARY 3 SNMP message(s): 0 ENCRYPTED, 3 PLAINTEXT

  <-- Three stimuli produced three traps, each about 5 s after its stimulus.  That agrees
      with the `Notification Interval 5 secs` the DUT reports.
  <-- The notification is the right one.  `snmpTrapOID.0 = 1.0.8802.1.1.2.0.0.1` is
      lldpRemTablesChange from the IEEE 802.1AB LLDP-MIB.  A v2c notification is
      identified by the VALUE of snmpTrapOID.0, which is why `--values` was used.
  <-- The varbinds say which change happened, and they agree with each other.  Traps #1
      and #2 share Inserts 9 while Deletes goes 4 to 5, which is the shutdown-frame
      delete.  Trap #3 shows Inserts 9 to 10, the second insert, with Deletes unchanged.
  <-- The trap came from the DUT's own vlan10 address 10.38.22.34, to the configured
      host, with the configured community.

  The control: the same stimulus with notifications off.
